(iii) the symmetrised (descent) architecture, hard ceiling, u_j = 1:
      entry log(256|s|) > tau -> sigma_m = 4, so asymptotically
      log(256|s|) > 4  <=>  normalised score > 4 - log 256 - 2 = -3.54518
      CDT's realised m = 14, u = (1,3): threshold -2.00041 (contour) / -2.49931 (ceiling)

(v) Galois trace: for a real-quadratic fold, log|x_2| - (-log lam2_norm)
      Beukers   : log|x_2| = +2.1392, -log lam2_norm = -1.3863  -> loss +3.5255
      level-5   : log|x_2| = +0.3266, -log lam2_norm = -2.0794  -> loss +2.4061
      sqrt-T    : log|x_2| = +0.3765, -log lam2_norm = -1.3863  -> loss +1.7627
